51:                                                ABSTRACT
53:                                               BACKGROUND // Mercury (Hg) is a toxic metal, and dietary exposure is the main one in humans, especially fish consumption. In
54:                                               order to reduce Hg exposure, maximum levels in fish products have been established. We aimed to describe total mercury (THg) and
55:                                               methylmercury (MeHg) concentrations in fish species consumed in Comunitat Valenciana, as well as factors associated and their
57:                                               METHODS // A retrospective descriptive study of Hg levels in fish meat samples in Comunitat Valenciana between 2011 and 2017 and
58:                                               their temporal trend was carried out, both in general and by fish groups. Data comes from Generalitat Valenciana’s Health Surveillance of
59:                                               Food Program. We created multivariate linear regression models to evaluate the association between sampling year, fish group and origin
61:                                               RESULTS // The median was 0.20 mg/kg for THg and 0.14 mg/kg for MeHg. Swordfish, fresh tuna/albacore and canned tuna, in that
62:                                               order, showed the highest concentrations. Global tendency of THg levels was descending when adjusting by swordfish annual percen-
63:                                               tage. When we analized the tendency in swordfish, we observed a 7% decrease on average per year.
64:                                               CONCLUSIONS // Global temporal trend of THg levels in fish in Comunitat Valenciana during the period 2011-2017 is descending after
65:                                               adjusting by the relative weight of swordfish over the total number of samples by year. We observe a descending tendency when
66:                                               studied by species (swordfish).
