Results from figure 1 revealed that Coffee waste has significant potential to adsorb Nickel (p<0.05) during 30 days of study and
after 30 days in presence of 0.3% of coffee waste, reduction of Nickel was not significant that approved that adsorption capacity
varied by considering the effects of various parameters like contact time, initial concentrations, and absorbent dose.




