wiki/sources/abaas2018-breast-milk-nickel.md:26:Abaas and colleagues measured nickel in breast milk from lactating mothers living in Hilla City, Iraq. The study is routeable for human-milk nickel exposure because it reports breast-milk nickel concentrations in ppb and evaluates associations with maternal and environmental variables. It is human-milk exposure evidence, not infant formula evidence.
